      "sourceTextSha256": "2fafd8886043c9f5ddb36296625516b56a16f91a4f58af9fcacb9059a03730ec",
      "text": "\n\nIf you enjoy ecotourism, hiking and simple campsites, this trip takes you to places you can only reach on foot. The main goal is the Lost City of the Tayrona people, hidden in the forested mountains near Santa Marta.\n\nSanta Marta is considered one of the main tourist centres on Colombia’s Caribbean coast. Spanish conquistador Rodrigo de Bastidas founded the city on 29 July 1525. After exploring Santa Marta, you set out on a multi-day trek across rivers and through forests, passing Indigenous villages and mountain camps. The trip ends with time to relax in Tayrona Natural Park.\n",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-98c5fe36c1a7",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
